  "step_3": "First, comparing the information considered: The decision reason relies on the comparison of skewness, specifically the proportion of probability on unfavorable outcomes. The individual did not consider or mention this aspect; instead, they focused on the closeness of probabilities and the higher monetary value. Second, comparing the decision rule: The reason prefers the more right-skewed lottery (A), but the individual chose A not because of skewness but because it offers a higher payoff under nearly equal probabilities. The individual’s justification is inconsistent with the skewness-based rule—choosing the higher payoff when probabilities are similar is not equivalent to preferring greater skewness. There is no indication that the individual evaluated or used the skewness criterion. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
